 {:db/id "q-87308" :question/id #uuid "610824ef-12b9-5ca4-a472-9a8e2ccc0745" :question/math-academy-id "q-87308" :question/problem "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events. Given that $P(B)=\\frac{18}{25}$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{4}{5},$ find $P(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events, then $P(A\\cap B)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, by the addition law, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B) \\\\ P(A) & =P(A\\cup B)-P(B) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{18}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{20-18}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87308/ma-source-field/e1f1e3e81c7417475212de78cd356cab2f9e27f3d05dc9b41cb071c67f94016a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
