 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "485dd702-22ef-5672-ba6d-aa433fac1c74"] :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${3}^{4x}{x}^{2}\\ge {3}^{4x+1}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{4x}{x}^{2} & \\ge {3}^{4x+1}x \\\\ {3}^{4x}{x}^{2}-{3}^{4x+1}x & \\ge 0 \\\\ {3}^{4x}({x}^{2}-3x) & \\ge 0 \\\\ {3}^{4x}x(x-3) & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{4x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x-3)\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=0$ and $x=3.$ The parabola is at or above the $x$-axis when $x\\le 0$ or $x\\ge 3.$\n\n![](images/3b/3bfb82543e7c05d0ca0b8f6c6973025400ad1253acbc57214173dbd3e8c37fef.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is  $x\\le 0$ or $x\\ge 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87772/ma-source-field/5489b4175c3dcfecc6b09e23cbda27c2a437e4769d97d80ddbb96860f49bf4ca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
