 {:db/id "q-87862" :question/id #uuid "019afbc4-64db-5396-aa9e-b5972e6733b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-87862" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-{2}^{6x-1}<{12}^{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since ${12}^{x}$ is always positive and $-{2}^{6x-1}$ is always negative, we always have\n\n$$\n-{2}^{6x-1}<{12}^{x}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the given inequality is satisfied by all real values of $x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87862/ma-source-field/abee843003c117324e16ce5e59a889aa6ba50a39134143f88264525c64b6ff05"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
