 {:db/id "q-89821/ma-source-field/dab9a6507124b2932716effe544c72386157d7ff39c3f6177637178d1f9c4965" :answer-field/id #uuid "aea651d3-f2f0-5676-bbf4-bf4713440432" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-89821/ma-source-field/dab9a6507124b2932716effe544c72386157d7ff39c3f6177637178d1f9c4965/d14a7de1ffe536ad06e316566281247f7d6e0c2112b6da7d1070b45512fb17f1" "q-89821/ma-source-field/dab9a6507124b2932716effe544c72386157d7ff39c3f6177637178d1f9c4965/a6cfffac6c7b189f0dbf6c99859c9ccfe97f3d05f4c38502c55711db8a826ebb" "q-89821/ma-source-field/dab9a6507124b2932716effe544c72386157d7ff39c3f6177637178d1f9c4965/207ddfaabe790159069c5bb80af6ed48b5f27862e8deea6637117542854104a1" "q-89821/ma-source-field/dab9a6507124b2932716effe544c72386157d7ff39c3f6177637178d1f9c4965/df14f13e85e41dbe61aa30dfc658dfc4f4dc049eb66b26ba8d1749593d02d57e" "q-89821/ma-source-field/dab9a6507124b2932716effe544c72386157d7ff39c3f6177637178d1f9c4965/ee942ade405838fbb9a48eac484208bd7ddcabcabf3a39e1a5b595a63b7d5012"] :answer-field/correct "q-89821/ma-source-field/dab9a6507124b2932716effe544c72386157d7ff39c3f6177637178d1f9c4965/df14f13e85e41dbe61aa30dfc658dfc4f4dc049eb66b26ba8d1749593d02d57e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-89821" :question/id #uuid "c32439a8-2f0a-52f2-ba4c-04ee07df7da8" :question/math-academy-id "q-89821" :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}=\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s+3}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,s>2 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3},\\,s>-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s+3}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}$ is $f(t)=2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-89821/ma-source-field/dab9a6507124b2932716effe544c72386157d7ff39c3f6177637178d1f9c4965"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
