 {:db/id "q-90323" :question/id #uuid "66b0d8c5-2487-53cc-b840-b06edcc12d56" :question/math-academy-id "q-90323" :question/problem "![](images/e8/e863789ff989ee1cb3d3fe6c22fe0d4daa1dac76d6fbfbebdad801006ca4c969.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=4x+3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<4x+3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{4}x-2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-90323/ma-source-field/0882fde74cdc1e7f5f278d0586ecc52a5ea1d03ec6837236b83302f536f43edf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
