 {:db/id "q-90580" :question/id #uuid "056f268e-6f23-5cca-ba50-28679fda2fed" :question/math-academy-id "q-90580" :question/problem "Which of the following polynomials are homogeneous?\n\nI. $f(x)=7{x}^{7}$\nII. $g(x,y)=x+y$\nIII. $h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z-2xyz+x{z}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's go through each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is homogeneous of degree $7.$  It is a polynomial of degree $7,$ with no terms of degree other than $7.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $1.$ It is a polynomial of degree $1,$ and all of its terms are of degree $1.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y,z)$ is  homogeneous of degree $3.$ It is a polynomial of degree $3,$ and all of its terms are of degree $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90580/ma-source-field/8c210d80a754a3e8daa8f72f7d3eff8cccbb8cf1244124274d82daba14e8850a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
