 {:db/id "q-91157" :question/id #uuid "bc8df3f8-8c99-53c4-bedf-bdbc4a64bd8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-91157" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -13 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above ${a}_{33}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -13 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-91157/ma-source-field/f2a74b05b31ee6f3f0a4f288cb60db9474a1d4734d84e1c966aabb3166e84fad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
