 {:db/id "q-93099" :question/id #uuid "deb7d641-51be-5b64-b25b-f4aefccbd21e" :question/math-academy-id "q-93099" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=-4\\sqrt[6]{5x-11}-8.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-4\\sqrt[6]{5x-11}-8=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4\\sqrt[6]{5x-11}-8 & =0 \\\\ -4\\sqrt[6]{5x-11} & =8 \\\\ \\sqrt[6]{5x-11} & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no root." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-93099/ma-source-field/b4e9bbe6ec5eb3cd92a58a1817e9bb0be9727bbcbb36840e97d93fbcc8e7d35a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
