 {:db/id "q-93686/ma-source-field/a74cfc62b781809c5171d773bd9c3a9d13ec4c442ffaa0809caf8c7c82cf92a0" :answer-field/id #uuid "e483500e-6827-5463-9cbf-bef05b8b48b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-93686/ma-source-field/a74cfc62b781809c5171d773bd9c3a9d13ec4c442ffaa0809caf8c7c82cf92a0/2dec7663fe429034b2417c766b2b4a9e560b82d6cadf05ec8ef926dd3b3002e6" "q-93686/ma-source-field/a74cfc62b781809c5171d773bd9c3a9d13ec4c442ffaa0809caf8c7c82cf92a0/dfa094e70e190b2f241471fec9cad67a8db580418f61715f6972442cb9fb1499" "q-93686/ma-source-field/a74cfc62b781809c5171d773bd9c3a9d13ec4c442ffaa0809caf8c7c82cf92a0/eda7f761ee11623a8365a7d6144b64cb04b3bce05981e4d0c45479aaefbfb5be" "q-93686/ma-source-field/a74cfc62b781809c5171d773bd9c3a9d13ec4c442ffaa0809caf8c7c82cf92a0/c7730ae35a98135d9d18831220445dcd43dfcb665dd9536c12ef017bb1b16d42" "q-93686/ma-source-field/a74cfc62b781809c5171d773bd9c3a9d13ec4c442ffaa0809caf8c7c82cf92a0/f1ce430c5f5445ca6979df2cfc116d47f756fbee9bef2b42cbe6b78c0a43e605"] :answer-field/correct "q-93686/ma-source-field/a74cfc62b781809c5171d773bd9c3a9d13ec4c442ffaa0809caf8c7c82cf92a0/c7730ae35a98135d9d18831220445dcd43dfcb665dd9536c12ef017bb1b16d42" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-93686" :question/id #uuid "ec1ebe33-0bb3-5ea6-a15e-48fad1ecf313" :question/math-academy-id "q-93686" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+9y=6{e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x},$ we have that $\\lambda =-3$ is the double root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $6{e}^{-3x}.$  In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $-3$, which coincides with the double root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{-3x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (2x-3{x}^{2}){e}^{-3x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (9{x}^{2}-12x+2){e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (9{x}^{2}-12x+2){e}^{-3x}+6(\\alpha (2x-3{x}^{2}){e}^{-3x})+9(\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}) & =6{e}^{-3x} \\\\ (9{x}^{2}-12x+2+12x-18{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2})\\alpha {e}^{-3x} & =6{e}^{-3x} \\\\ 2\\alpha {e}^{-3x} & =6{e}^{-3x} \\\\ 2\\alpha  & =6 \\\\ \\alpha  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93686/ma-source-field/a74cfc62b781809c5171d773bd9c3a9d13ec4c442ffaa0809caf8c7c82cf92a0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
