 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "ca11e17a-4464-5c54-bbb1-cb2d8dc175df"] :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n2{y}_{1}^{2}-\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} & =2([{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}]-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} & =2({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n2{y}_{1}^{2}-3{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $3\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93838/ma-source-field/a1270a7178c1462faa9e13c89e9417f595e2d757ff6328f900f2038ceb26bbf6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
