 {:db/id "q-94159" :question/id #uuid "8abbbd8d-56c6-5a50-8378-69e23e070d79" :question/math-academy-id "q-94159" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+18{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+18{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3})-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}))-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})^{2})-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-16{x}_{3}^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94159/ma-source-field/cb9e4f1bd5761f2b1f32ef02ad75350d8ad6529ad2c78d3ec731d7cd3e7e4fbd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
