 {:db/id "q-94179" :question/id #uuid "c34790ce-c36b-5dcb-a189-d84001cf999a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94179" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-{x}_{3}))+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2})+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+7{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2([{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2}]-4{x}_{3}^{2})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2(({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-4{x}_{3}^{2})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-8{x}_{3}^{2}+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-94179/ma-source-field/bf775581c0bcd36aed1f36a93e88fb92f2e379facf12b485903113436e600b2f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
